   943	          # PHYSICAL source confinement since round 7; the two HASH sites did
   944	          # not, and `_hash_file` follows symlinks exactly as `cp -p` does. A
   945	          # source whose leaf OR ancestor links to a regular file outside this
   946	          # checkout therefore hashed FOREIGN bytes, and the verdict flipped
   947	          # away from the conservative one: here to "MISSING (restorable)" for
   948	          # a file `_restore_file` would then refuse to write, and at the DRIFT
   949	          # site below to "baseline-stale" — a verdict that TELLS the operator
   950	          # to bless foreign bytes into the baseline by running upgrade.sh.
