     5	# GitHub Actions never reads it. Activation is an EXPLICIT adopter step
     6	# (plain `mv -n`, not `git mv`: on a fresh install the delivered file is
     7	# UNTRACKED so `git mv` fails — measured S344, PLAN-183 AC-2 — and `-n`
     8	# refuses to clobber a benchmarks.yml of your own — but on that collision
     9	# `mv -n` exits 0 WITHOUT moving, so the workflow stays INERT: check the
    10	# rename landed, or pick another name, before you commit):
    11	#   mv -n .github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template \
    12	#         .github/workflows/benchmarks.yml
    13	#
    14	# ONCE ACTIVATED THIS COSTS REAL MONEY ON YOUR OWN ACCOUNT. It requires the
    15	# repository secret ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (Settings -> Secrets and variables ->
    16	# Actions). Each run bills YOUR Anthropic account: one SUCCESSFUL response per
    17	# benchmark scenario per repetition — the runner makes up to three request
    18	# attempts on a rate limit or API error, so request volume can exceed that
    19	# count — for every benchmark YAML under
    20	# `.claude/skills/**/benchmarks/`. The runner refuses any single benchmark
    21	# YAML whose ESTIMATED cost exceeds $1.00 unless invoked with
    22	# --allow-expensive — a per-invocation cap, not a budget; there is NO
    23	# aggregate workflow-wide cap, and the paths filter below is the only
    24	# throttle on how often the whole job runs. With no secret configured the
    25	# job skips visibly and bills nothing.
    26	#
    27	# SELF-CONTAINED BY CONTRACT (PLAN-183 W2 / finding A3): every script this
    28	# workflow calls must be one the installer actually delivers.
    29	# `.claude/scripts/run-skill-benchmark.py` ships via
    30	# install.sh::install_scripts_selective(). The framework's own
    31	# `.github/scripts/` is NOT installed, so nothing here may reference it.
    32	#
    33	# Only runs on changes to skill benchmarks, the runner, or this workflow
    34	# itself. Per PLAN-002 §11-bis Q2: paths filter keeps docs/plans/hooks PRs
    35	# from paying API cost.
    36	on:
