     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""statusline-ceo.py — Claude Code statusLine renderer + telemetry sidecar (PLAN-135 W5 O4).
     3	
     4	Reads the Claude Code statusLine stdin JSON contract, renders ONE status
     5	line on stdout, and tees a JSON snapshot ("sidecar") to the project state
     6	dir (ADR-001 convention) for fail-soft consumption by:
     7	
     8	  * ``measure_multiplier`` (PLAN-128 §7) — live /usage-equivalent quota
     9	    snapshot next to the post-hoc transcript math;
    10	  * ``check_budget``       (hook)        — advisory quota warning line.
    11	
    12	## stdin contract (tolerant — absent/unknown fields degrade, never crash)
    13	
    14	Claude Code pipes a JSON object on every refresh. Known fields consumed:
    15	
    16	    model.display_name / model.id
    17	    workspace.project_dir / cwd
    18	    session_id, version
    19	    cost.total_cost_usd / total_lines_added / total_lines_removed
    20	    exceeds_200k_tokens                                  (bool)
    21	    context_window | context  (used/max tokens OR used_percentage)
    22	    rate_limits   — the /usage-equivalent buckets. Verified against the
    23	                    Claude Code statusLine contract (code.claude.com/docs,
    24	                    fetched 2026-06-13): nested
    25	                    ``rate_limits.{five_hour,seven_day}.{used_percentage,
    26	                    resets_at}`` where ``used_percentage`` is 0-100 and
    27	                    ``resets_at`` is UNIX EPOCH SECONDS (int). Present only
    28	                    for Claude.ai Pro/Max subscribers after the first API
    29	                    response; each window may be independently absent. The
    30	                    Agent-SDK credit bucket (post-2026-06-15) is NOT a field
    31	                    on this contract — recorded as a forward-looking bucket
    32	                    alias only; if Claude Code adds it under rate_limits the
    33	                    generic parser picks it up untruncated. A flat
    34	                    ``{used_percentage, resets_at}`` is also tolerated.
    35	
    36	PROBE (pending-owner, $0 — the status line runs LOCALLY and consumes NO
    37	API tokens, per the Claude Code docs): set ``CEO_STATUSLINE_DEBUG=1`` and
    38	run a live session — the raw stdin JSON is teed to ``<sidecar>.debug.json``
    39	so the live field shapes can be pinned against a real harness, in particular
    40	that ``rate_limits`` is present (it appears only for Claude.ai Pro/Max after
    41	the first API response) and whether the Agent-SDK credit bucket surfaces
    42	there post-2026-06-15 (Doctrine 3: verify the knob routes). The field
    43	contract itself is already verified from code.claude.com/docs (2026-06-13).
    44	
    45	## Sidecar (schema ``statusline-sidecar/v1``)
    46	
    47	Path resolution (mirror of ``_lib/audit_emit._audit_dir()``, ADR-001):
    48	
    49	    $CEO_STATUSLINE_SIDECAR                              (full-path override)
    50	    else <audit-dir>/state/statusline-snapshot.json
    51	    where <audit-dir> = $CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR
    52	                        or _lib.runtime_paths.runtime_state_dir()
    53	                           = $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE, else
    54	                             ~/.claude/projects/<native-slug>
    55	                           (the project's own path with `/` -> `-`)
    56	
    57	    On a partial upgrade where `_lib/runtime_paths` is absent, the resolution
    58	    degrades to the legacy `~/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration` and says so
    59	    on stderr. Operators reading this contract to find a sidecar: on a normal
    60	    complete install it is under the NATIVE-SLUG dir, not the legacy one.
    61	
    62	Atomic write: tmp file in the same dir + ``os.replace``. Content is
    63	numbers / enum-ish ids only — free text from stdin is never echoed.
    64	
    65	TRUST TIER (residual, recorded verbatim in PLAN-135 §W5): "the sidecar is
    66	an unauthenticated local JSON read as governance input — same trust tier
    67	as other local state; integrity posture = follow-up if it ever gates a
    68	decision." Consumers MUST stay advisory-only on this input.
    69	
    70	## Closed-enum audit action
    71	
    72	``statusline_sidecar_write`` — declared in PLAN-135
    73	``staged/w5/actions-added.md`` (folded into ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` + SPEC at
    74	arc consolidation). Emitted fail-soft via ``_lib.audit_emit.emit_generic``
    75	and DEBOUNCED: only when the material digest changes AND at least
    76	``CEO_STATUSLINE_EMIT_INTERVAL_S`` (default 300) elapsed since the last
    77	emit. Pre-ceremony, ``emit_generic`` drops the unknown action with a
    78	breadcrumb — bounded by the same debounce, so no flood either way.
    79	
    80	## Env surface
    81	
    82	    CEO_STATUSLINE_SIDECAR           full sidecar path override
    83	    CEO_STATUSLINE_DISABLE=1         render-only (no sidecar, no emit)
    84	    CEO_STATUSLINE_EMIT=0            sidecar write but no audit emit
    85	    CEO_STATUSLINE_EMIT_INTERVAL_S   emit debounce floor seconds (default 300)
    86	    CEO_STATUSLINE_DEBUG=1           tee raw stdin JSON to <sidecar>.debug.json
    87	    CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR                state-dir base (matches audit_log.py)
    88	
    89	## Fail-soft contract
    90	
    91	ANY internal error → minimal one-line render + exit 0. A status line must
    92	never break the session (same posture as hook fail-open, ADR-005).
    93	
    94	Stdlib only. Python >= 3.9.
    95	"""
