   295	  `validate.yml.template` in a throwaway target and runs its steps in
   296	  order, one `bash -eo pipefail` per step, stopping at the first red. Any
   297	  workflow shape outside the frozen subset is a parse FAILURE, never a
   298	  vacuous green. Runs on Linux with `CI=true` or
   299	  `CEO_SMOKE_EXECUTE_CI=1`; elsewhere it lists the steps with a note.
   300	- **The delivered template changed accordingly:** it is SHA-pinned
   301	  (`actions/checkout`), honors a `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` repository variable
   302	  as a kill switch, raises its own timeout 5 → 15 minutes, installs PyYAML
   303	  in CI when it is absent and FAILS the YAML catalog syntax check if no
   304	  parser can be had (a syntax gate that skips silently is a gate that
   305	  fails open; a slim offline runner therefore goes red, by design), and
   306	  verifies the SHA-256 of the actionlint release asset before running it.
   307	  It ships INERT with a `.template` suffix; activation is still an
   308	  explicit `mv -n` you perform.
   309	
   310	### Added — `claude-fable-5-1` in the model allowlist (`ab56e76`)
   311	
   312	- `claude-fable-5-1` joins `availableModels` in `.claude/settings.json`
   313	  and in the maintainer/base settings template (the advisory `user`
   314	  profile deliberately carries no `availableModels`). Adopting a new model is
   315	  deliberately never automatic: the VETO floor, the pins and the agent
   316	  definitions stay Owner-signed by design (ADR-149 remains the single
   317	  source for the model catalog).
   318	
   319	### Fixed — seven VETO-bearing skills were demoted to name-only (`b7dad83`)
   320	
   321	- `kill-switches`, `latency-budgets`, `equity-research`,
   322	  `financial-correctness-and-math`, `financial-display`,
   323	  `prediction-markets` and `trading-execution` were listed under
   324	  `skillOverrides` as `name-only`, which withholds their body from the
   325	  agent — including from the veto paths that are supposed to read them.
   200	  this account class that default is currently inside the working set; the
   201	  picker surface is recorded here so the probe checks it rather than
   202	  assuming it.
   203	- A blocked subagent `model:` override **falls back silently** to the
   204	  inherited/default model (documented 2.1.172 semantics) rather than
   205	  failing the spawn — fine for the routing floor, but it means frontmatter
   206	  pins are not self-verifying; the spawn gate (`check_agent_spawn` /
   207	  `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`) remains the enforcement layer for VETO personas.
   208	
   209	## Amendment 2 (S338 — Fable 5.1 joins the working set; floor, fallback and pin unchanged)
   210	
   211	> Authored S338 (2026-09-01) under PLAN-169 (fleet-currency remit, W2.10
   212	> class cure: functional surfaces DERIVE from this ADR). Ratified by the
   213	> Owner via AskUserQuestion at the S338 opening — **route (c) of three**:
   214	> working-set append only. Lands through the `wave-fable51` sentinel ceremony
   215	> (`.claude/plans/PLAN-169/wave-fable51-approved.md`).
   216	
   217	### A2.1 Facts the amendment rests on (models overview, fetched 2026-09-01)
   218	
   219	- Claude Fable 5.1 launched 2026-09-01 alongside Mythos 5.1 (same
   220	  underlying model; Fable carries the additional dual-use safety
   221	  measures and is the generally available one).
   222	- **API id = alias = `claude-fable-5-1`** — dateless. Every id from the
   223	  4.6 generation on is a pinned snapshot, so a date suffix must NEVER be
   224	  appended (the S337 recon measured 233 files citing `claude-fable-5`
   225	  and 0 citing the 5.1 id; the cure is this data change, not a hunt).
   226	- $10 in / $50 out per MTok (equal to Fable 5); 1M context; 128K max
   227	  output; knowledge cutoff June 2026; adaptive always-on thinking;
   228	  retirement no earlier than 2027-09-01.
   229	- **Cache hits on Fable 5.1 are 0.025x the base input price ($0.25/MTok)**
   230	  — the pricing page (fetched 2026-09-01) resolves the conflict the S337
   231	  recon recorded between the models overview (0.1x) and the launch note;
   232	  every other model keeps the standard 0.1x. `budget-summary.py` is the
   233	  ONE cost surface that prices cache reads (input-equivalents), so it
   234	  gains a per-model multiplier instead of the flat 0.10x that would have
   235	  overstated Fable 5.1 cache reads 4x (codex rail r1 P2).
   236	- `claude-fable-5` remains available as LEGACY: the change is ADDITIVE.
   237	
   238	### A2.2 Decision
   239	
   240	1. `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET` gains `claude-fable-5-1` **at the end**
   241	   (A1.1 order rule — no reorder, no removal). The generated
   242	   `availableModels` mirrors (`.claude/settings.json`,
   243	   `templates/settings/settings.base.json`) follow byte-for-byte via
   244	   `generate-available-models.py`; every INDEPENDENT mirror bound by
   245	   `test_adr149_validator_parity.py` (validate-governance case-arm,
   246	   `tier_policy_cli.VALID_MODEL_IDS`, `smoke-install-parity.sh`
   247	   `ALLOWED_MODELS`) carries the same append in the same patch.
   248	2. `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` is **unchanged**: Fable 5.1 is selectable, not
   249	   VETO-eligible. Routes (a)/(b) — floor membership with or without
   250	   migrating the six `agents/*.md` pins — stay open as a FUTURE amendment
   251	   that the Owner may ratify after measuring the 5.1 verdict quality;
   252	   nothing here pre-empts it.
   253	3. `FALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN` is **unchanged** (`claude-opus-5`).
   254	4. The session-default `model` pin stays `claude-opus-5` in all three
   255	   adopter-facing mirrors. Flipping it is a SEPARATE decision with its own
   256	   blast radius (adopter default cost x2; `upgrade.sh` pin migration;
   257	   `test_template_dogfood_parity.py` EXPECTED_PIN) and is not made here.
   258	   A maintainer who wants 5.1 as the session default on ONE machine sets
   259	   it in `.claude/settings.local.json` (highest-precedence project layer;
   260	   the generator `--check` resolves that overlay, A1.2).
   261	5. `scripts/upgrade.sh` learns a **`superseded`** list for the
   262	   `availableModels` leaf: the 6-id array that v1.2.0 and v1.3.0 SHIPPED
   263	   is a frozen historical literal (same doctrine as the pair-rail
   264	   `OLD_PAIR_RAIL_CAPS`). Without it the 3-state migration would read
   265	   every v1.2.0/v1.3.0 adopter as ADOPTER-CUSTOMIZED and never deliver

