   245	# rail round-4 F3 — the READER being present is not the TABLE being present.
   246	# _wbm_route_src answers rc=1 ("no row for this destination") when the table is
   247	# missing or unreadable, and every call site below answers rc=1 with the
   248	# identity fallback `$SOURCE_DIR/$rel`. On a partial checkout that is defect D4
   249	# arriving through an absent file instead of a wrong branch — and D4 does not
   250	# merely misclassify: `_restore_file` COPIES. MEASURED pre-cure (S327): with
   251	# the table removed, `--repair` of a deleted `docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md` wrote
   252	# the ROOT homonym's bytes into the adopter tree, and the same path applied to
   253	# `.github/CODEOWNERS` copies THIS repo's live maintainer file — the exact
   254	# contamination class PLAN-183 A3 closed elsewhere.
   255	#
   256	# So the table is a REQUIRED input, asserted once, before any verdict is
